{"id":"mahabharata-8-036","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":36,"title":"षट्त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 36 · The battle in the dust","summary":{"en":"The warriors, filled with hate, kill one another with weapons of all kinds, and the elephants hurl away the arrows that strike them. In the confusion no one can tell friend from foe, and the Kaurava army breaks.","kn":"ದ್ವೇಷತುಂಬಿದ ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯರು ವಿಧವಿಧ ಆಯುಧಗಳಿಂದ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಆನೆಗಳು ತಮಗೆ ತಾಗಿದ ಬಾಣಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡವುತ್ತವೆ. ಗೊಂದಲದಲ್ಲಿ ಮಿತ್ರ-ಶತ್ರು ತಿಳಿಯದೆ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಒಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"द्वेष से भरे क्षत्रिय नाना शस्त्रों से एक-दूसरे को मारते हैं और हाथी अपने ऊपर लगे बाण झटक देते हैं। अव्यवस्था में मित्र-शत्रु की पहचान नहीं रहती और कौरव सेना टूट जाती है।","te":"ద్వేషంతో నిండిన క్షత్రియులు వివిధ ఆయుధాలతో ఒకరినొకరు చంపుకుంటారు; ఏనుగులు తమకు తగిలిన బాణాలను విదిలిస్తాయి. గందరగోళంలో మిత్రశత్రువులు తెలియక కౌరవసేన విరిగిపోతుంది.","ta":"பகை நிறைந்த க்ஷத்திரியர் பல ஆயுதங்களால் ஒருவரை ஒருவர் கொல்கின்றனர்; யானைகள் தம்மேல் பட்ட அம்புகளை உதறுகின்றன. குழப்பத்தில் நண்பர் பகைவர் தெரியாமல் கௌரவப் படை உடைகிறது.","ml":"വിദ്വേഷം നിറഞ്ഞ യോദ്ധാക്കൾ എല്ലാത്തരം ആയുധങ്ങളാലും പരസ്പരം കൊല്ലുന്നു; തങ്ങളെ തറയ്ക്കുന്ന അമ്പുകളെ ആനകൾ തട്ടിക്കളയുന്നു. പൊടിപടലത്തിൽ സുഹൃത്തേത് ശത്രുവേത് എന്ന് ആർക്കും തിരിച്ചറിയാനാകുന്നില്ല; കൗരവസേന തകരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.36; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"क्षत्रियास्ते महाराज परस्परवधैषिणः ।\nअन्योन्यं समरे जघ्नुः कृतवैराः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, those kshatriyas, each bent on killing the other, fought one another in the battle, their enmity now open."}},{"n":2,"text":"रथौघाश्च हयौघाश्च नरौघाश्च समन्ततः ।\nगजौघाश्च महाराज संसक्ताः स्म परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, masses of chariots, horses, men and elephants pressed in on every side, jammed against one another."}},{"n":3,"text":"गदानां परिघाणां च कणपानां च सर्पताम् ।\nप्रासानां भिण्डिपालानां भुशुण्डीनां च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that terrible fight we saw clubs, iron bars, kanapas, hurtling spears, lances, bhindipalas and bhushundis falling all around."}},{"n":4,"text":"संपातं चान्वपश्याम संग्रामे भृशदारुणे ।\nशलभा इव संपेतुः समन्ताच्छरवृष्टयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showers of arrows dropped from every side like swarms of locusts."}},{"n":5,"text":"नागा नागान्समासाद्य व्यधमन्त परस्परम् ।\nहया हयांश्च समरे रथिनो रथिनस्तथा ।\nपत्तयः पत्तिसंघैश्च हयसंघैर्हयास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants met elephants and tore at each other; horses fought horses, charioteers fought charioteers, foot soldiers fought troops of foot soldiers, and horse-troops fought horse-troops."}},{"n":6,"text":"पत्तयो रथमातङ्गान्रथा हस्त्यश्वमेव च ।\nनागाश्च समरे त्र्यङ्गं ममृदुः शीघ्रगा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, foot soldiers crushed chariots and elephants, chariots crushed elephants and horses, and swift elephants trampled the three limbs of the army in the battle."}},{"n":7,"text":"पततां तत्र शूराणां क्रोशतां च परस्परम् ।\nघोरमायोधनं जज्ञे पशूनां वैशसं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the heroes fell and shouted at one another, a dreadful battlefield arose, like the slaughter of cattle at a sacrifice."}},{"n":8,"text":"रुधिरेण समास्तीर्णा भाति भारत मेदिनी ।\nशक्रगोपगणाकीर्णा प्रावृषीव यथा धरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, the earth, covered in blood and scattered with red velvet mites, looked like the ground in the rainy season."}},{"n":9,"text":"यथा वा वाससी शुक्ले महारजनरञ्जिते ।\nबिभृयाद्युवतिः श्यामा तद्वदासीद्वसुंधरा ।\nमांसशोणितचित्रेव शातकौम्भमयीव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or the earth looked like a dark young woman wearing two white garments dyed deep red, streaked with flesh and blood, as if made of gold."}},{"n":10,"text":"छिन्नानां चोत्तमाङ्गानां बाहूनां चोरुभिः सह ।\nकुण्डलानां प्रविद्धानां भूषणानां च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, severed heads, arms with thighs, flung-off earrings and ornaments fell there on the ground."}},{"n":11,"text":"निष्काणामधिसूत्राणां शरीराणां च धन्विनाम् ।\nवर्मणां सपताकानां संघास्तत्रापतन्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gold necklaces, belts, the bodies of archers and armour with banners, in heaps, dropped to the earth."}},{"n":12,"text":"गजान्गजाः समासाद्य विषाणाग्रैरदारयन् ।\nविषाणाभिहतास्ते च भ्राजन्ते द्विरदा यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants came against elephants and ripped at each other with the tips of their tusks; struck by the tusks, they shone like glittering beasts."}},{"n":13,"text":"रुधिरेणावसिक्ताङ्गा गैरिकप्रस्रवा इव ।\nयथा भ्राजन्ति स्यन्दन्तः पर्वता धातुमण्डिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their bodies drenched in blood they looked like mountains streaked with minerals, running with red streams."}},{"n":14,"text":"तोमरान्गजिभिर्मुक्तान्प्रतीपानास्थितान्बहून् ।\nहस्तैर्विचेरुस्ते नागा बभञ्जुश्चापरे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants flung away the spears hurled by riders and, facing them, wandered about; some seized them in their trunks and others broke them."}},{"n":15,"text":"नाराचैश्छिन्नवर्माणो भ्राजन्ते स्म गजोत्तमाः ।\nहिमागमे महाराज व्यभ्रा इव महीधराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, the finest elephants, their armour cut by iron arrows, shone like cloudless mountains when winter comes."}},{"n":16,"text":"शरैः कनकपुङ्खैस्तु चिता रेजुर्गजोत्तमाः ।\nउल्काभिः संप्रदीप्ताग्राः पर्वता इव मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, the best elephants, covered with arrows with golden shafts, shone like mountains whose peaks are blazing with torches."}},{"n":17,"text":"केचिदभ्याहता नागा नागैर्नगनिभा भुवि ।\nनिपेतुः समरे तस्मिन्पक्षवन्त इवाद्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some elephants, struck down by other elephants, fell in that battle like mountains, as if winged mountains had dropped to earth."}},{"n":18,"text":"अपरे प्राद्रवन्नागाः शल्यार्ता व्रणपीडिताः ।\nप्रतिमानैश्च कुम्भैश्च पेतुरुर्व्यां महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other elephants, tormented by arrow-points and wounds, fled, and in the great fight they fell to the ground along with their frontlets and ornaments."}},{"n":19,"text":"निषेदुः सिंहवच्चान्ये नदन्तो भैरवान्रवान् ।\nमम्लुश्च बहवो राजंश्चुकूजुश्चापरे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others sank down like lions, bellowing fearful cries; many, O king, grew faint and others trumpeted."}},{"n":20,"text":"हयाश्च निहता बाणैः स्वर्णभाण्डपरिच्छदाः ।\nनिषेदुश्चैव मम्लुश्च बभ्रमुश्च दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses killed by arrows, with their golden trappings, sank down, fainted, or whirled around in all ten directions."}},{"n":21,"text":"अपरे कृष्यमाणाश्च विवेष्टन्तो महीतले ।\nभावान्बहुविधांश्चक्रुस्ताडिताः शरतोमरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, dragged along and struck by arrows and spears, rolled on the ground and made many different movements."}},{"n":22,"text":"नरास्तु निहता भूमौ कूजन्तस्तत्र मारिष ।\nदृष्ट्वा च बान्धवानन्ये पितॄनन्ये पितामहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, men lay slain on the ground, crying out there; some, seeing their kinsmen, others their fathers and grandfathers, called out."}},{"n":23,"text":"धावमानान्परांश्चैव दृष्ट्वान्ये तत्र भारत ।\nगोत्रनामानि ख्यातानि शशंसुरितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, others who saw enemies rushing at them there called out to one another their clan and family names."}},{"n":24,"text":"तेषां छिन्ना महाराज भुजाः कनकभूषणाः ।\nउद्वेष्टन्ते विवेष्टन्ते पतन्ते चोत्पतन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, their severed arms with golden ornaments writhed, twisted, fell and leaped up."}},{"n":25,"text":"निपतन्ति तथा भूमौ स्फुरन्ति च सहस्रशः ।\nवेगांश्चान्ये रणे चक्रुः स्फुरन्त इव पन्नगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They fell to the ground and quivered in their thousands; some, in the battle, made movements like twitching snakes."}},{"n":26,"text":"ते भुजा भोगिभोगाभाश्चन्दनाक्ता विशां पते ।\nलोहितार्द्रा भृशं रेजुस्तपनीयध्वजा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of men, those arms, like the bodies of serpents, smeared with sandal and wet with blood, shone brightly like banners of gold."}},{"n":27,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा घोरे संकुले सर्वतोदिशम् ।\nअविज्ञाताः स्म युध्यन्ते विनिघ्नन्तः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that dreadful fight went on, crowded in every direction, men fought unrecognized, striking one another down."}},{"n":28,"text":"भौमेन रजसा कीर्णे शस्त्रसंपातसंकुले ।\nनैव स्वे न परे राजन्व्यज्ञायन्त तमोवृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, filled with the dust of the earth and the fall of weapons, wrapped in darkness, neither their own men nor the enemy could be told apart."}},{"n":29,"text":"तथा तदभवद्युद्धं घोररूपं भयानकम् ।\nशोणितोदा महानद्यः प्रसस्रुस्तत्र चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So that battle became terrible and fearsome; great rivers of blood flowed there again and again."}},{"n":30,"text":"शीर्षपाषाणसंछन्नाः केशशैवलशाद्वलाः ।\nअस्थिसंघातसंकीर्णा धनुःशरवरोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were covered with heads for stones, with hair for moss and grass, and strewn with heaps of bones; the best of bows and arrows lay in them."}},{"n":31,"text":"मांसकर्दमपङ्काश्च शोणितौघाः सुदारुणाः ।\nनदीः प्रवर्तयामासुर्यमराष्ट्रविवर्धनीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dreadful floods of blood, with flesh for mud and slime, produced rivers that swelled the realm of Yama."}},{"n":32,"text":"ता नद्यो घोररूपाश्च नयन्त्यो यमसादनम् ।\nअवगाढा मज्जयन्त्यः क्षत्रस्याजनयन्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those fearsome rivers, bearing men toward Yama's house, drowned those who entered them and brought fear to the kshatriyas."}},{"n":33,"text":"क्रव्यादानां नरव्याघ्र नर्दतां तत्र तत्र ह ।\nघोरमायोधनं जज्ञे प्रेतराजपुरोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tiger among men, where flesh-eaters roared here and there, the battlefield became fearsome, like the city of the king of the dead."}},{"n":34,"text":"उत्थितान्यगणेयानि कबन्धानि समन्ततः ।\nनृत्यन्ति वै भूतगणाः संतृप्ता मांसशोणितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Countless headless trunks rose up on every side, and troops of spirits, sated with flesh and blood, danced."}},{"n":35,"text":"पीत्वा च शोणितं तत्र वसां पीत्वा च भारत ।\nमेदोमज्जावसातृप्तास्तृप्ता मांसस्य चैव हि ।\nधावमानाश्च दृश्यन्ते काकगृध्रबलास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, crows, vultures and herons were seen running about, drinking blood and fat, filled with marrow and fat and flesh."}},{"n":36,"text":"शूरास्तु समरे राजन्भयं त्यक्त्वा सुदुस्त्यजम् ।\nयोधव्रतसमाख्याताश्चक्रुः कर्माण्यभीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the heroes in the battle, giving up the fear that is so hard to give up, did their deeds as if unafraid, keeping the vow of warriors."}},{"n":37,"text":"शरशक्तिसमाकीर्णे क्रव्यादगणसंकुले ।\nव्यचरन्त गणैः शूराः ख्यापयन्तः स्वपौरुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the field strewn with arrows and spears and crowded with flesh-eaters, the heroes moved in bands, proclaiming their own manliness."}},{"n":38,"text":"अन्योन्यं श्रावयन्ति स्म नामगोत्राणि भारत ।\nपितृनामानि च रणे गोत्रनामानि चाभितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, they called out to one another their names and clans, and in the battle the names of their fathers and of their families on all sides."}},{"n":39,"text":"श्रावयन्तो हि बहवस्तत्र योधा विशां पते ।\nअन्योन्यमवमृद्नन्तः शक्तितोमरपट्टिशैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, many warriors there called out in this way while trampling one another with spears, lances and battle-axes."}},{"n":40,"text":"वर्तमाने तदा युद्धे घोररूपे सुदारुणे ।\nव्यषीदत्कौरवी सेना भिन्ना नौरिव सागरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that dreadful, very terrible battle was going on, the Kuru army sank down like a broken ship in the ocean."}}]}]}